{"title":"1992 IMO Problems/Problem 6","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1992_IMO_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>For each positive integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/6/0965bf432b818b46740e3cd4d042899628c7ad0e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S(n)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"35\" height=\"18\" /> is defined to be the greatest integer such that, for every positive integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/d/d/dddc539a3077664ca1d8a17545ff75249a3ae6d9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k \\le S(n)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"73\" height=\"20\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/6/a/a6a719ab858b04f20ad51958e6fb53a1e8ba477a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n^{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"17\" /> can be written as the sum of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> positive squares.\n</p><p>(a) Prove that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/0/4b0e9e4a3fbefbb47faab6d47aebbf53333d8104.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S(n) \\le n^{2}-14$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"122\" height=\"21\" /> for each <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/1/b/d1b94ea0cc3ac2d353695f157196aed47896fefc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n \\ge 4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>(b) Find an integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/b/6/eb6e9f988b61393d372d1cc8ca8f79238f5741ca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S(n)=n^{2}-14$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"122\" height=\"21\" />.\n</p><p>(c) Prove that there are infinitely many integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/b/6/eb6e9f988b61393d372d1cc8ca8f79238f5741ca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S(n)=n^{2}-14$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"122\" height=\"21\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1992_IMO_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Problem (a)\nThe number <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/0/6006bba637eef443381fbaff768fa62d9ff41e62.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"17\" /> can be written as the sum of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/0/6006bba637eef443381fbaff768fa62d9ff41e62.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"17\" /> positive squares: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/4/e/c4e104894ef5552f2e2f769b41e3b8324d90726e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n^2 = \\underbrace{1^2 + 1^2 + \\dots + 1^2}_{n^2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -27px\" width=\"182\" height=\"43\" />.\nAny representation of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/0/6006bba637eef443381fbaff768fa62d9ff41e62.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"17\" /> as a sum of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/4/844f547541c1c08df3d6ebc7fb5f0a38627451f8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k &lt; n^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"54\" height=\"18\" /> positive squares can be obtained from this maximal sum by grouping multiple <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/1/c716d1dc907ae6b51cb0f545664c89d58b6b67d9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"15\" height=\"15\" /> terms into larger squares. Replacing <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> copies of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/1/c716d1dc907ae6b51cb0f545664c89d58b6b67d9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"15\" height=\"15\" /> with a single square <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/6/b/76b2878564ab19b80abb21ba964abe90fe120846.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^2$\" width=\"16\" height=\"15\" /> (where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/a/98a3d392cdeb37c1a01fc43c316fc3c83fd6c381.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m=x^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"17\" />) reduces the total number of terms by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/0/8506cdfc2f65bfb3e57e2e74ad11cde48c0ff863.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^2 - 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"48\" height=\"15\" />.\nThus, for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/0/6006bba637eef443381fbaff768fa62d9ff41e62.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"17\" /> to be the sum of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> positive squares, the difference <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/0/4/c04e90443dc57a12381aad1c55b1f06198ba23ef.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\Delta = n^2 - k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"92\" height=\"18\" /> must be expressible as a sum of integers from the set <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/9/5/3952d34c3af39f0d3fdabdbb5ec0958c14601ab0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$R = \\{x^2 - 1 \\mid x \\ge 2\\} = \\{3, 8, 15, 24, \\dots\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"320\" height=\"21\" />.\n</p><p>We examine which integers cannot be formed by sums of elements in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/f/eff43e84f8a3bcf7b6965f0a3248bc4d3a9d0cd4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$R$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />:\nThe representable integers are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/1/2/1124752d10a33cd2d8435d7a3b498e8b0399856a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0, 3, 6, 8, 9, 11, 12, 14, \\dots$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"191\" height=\"17\" />.\nThe integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/0/030e19e4e2f1c074127cb50581e8496470c5419f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$13$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> cannot be expressed as a sum of elements of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/f/eff43e84f8a3bcf7b6965f0a3248bc4d3a9d0cd4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$R$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> (<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/0/030e19e4e2f1c074127cb50581e8496470c5419f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$13$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> is not in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/f/eff43e84f8a3bcf7b6965f0a3248bc4d3a9d0cd4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$R$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/3/7/737dce881325119ba4bd5b0e63565cccf7aaf1be.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$13-3=10 \\notin R$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"130\" height=\"17\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/3/f/53fc0ebfb5815f9c9e55f175aec4a539b23c6017.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$13-8=5 \\notin R$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"121\" height=\"17\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/b/2/0b240d6c8acf2f19d0abf27c7ffa7b7813504231.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$13-3-3=7 \\notin R$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"152\" height=\"17\" />, etc.).\n</p><p>Consequently, it is impossible to obtain a representation with exactly <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/7/c/f7c947ce4ac073137e3527aece1fad6a6d5320d5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k = n^2 - 13$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"95\" height=\"18\" /> terms. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/6/0965bf432b818b46740e3cd4d042899628c7ad0e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S(n)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"35\" height=\"18\" /> requires that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/0/6006bba637eef443381fbaff768fa62d9ff41e62.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"17\" /> be the sum of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> squares for all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/d/d/dddc539a3077664ca1d8a17545ff75249a3ae6d9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k \\le S(n)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"73\" height=\"20\" />, the sequence of valid <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> breaks at or before <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/2/4/c24206c6806ecf2fd9a5af3ddb50232ba67fb40b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n^2 - 13$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" />.\nTherefore, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/2/c929a023ae874334c8a70ef6fed0b29b29dc86df.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S(n) &lt; n^2 - 13$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"122\" height=\"21\" />, which implies <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/c/8/cc8bc04b7a19499d7b25996fcd1f19f8ff84415b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S(n) \\le n^2 - 14$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"122\" height=\"21\" />.\n</p><p>Problem (b)\nFor <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/3/8/738855f6665f28ddccc59c3c3dc4e7ccdd33cbc6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S(n) = n^2 - 14$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"122\" height=\"21\" />, we require that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/0/6006bba637eef443381fbaff768fa62d9ff41e62.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"17\" /> be expressible as the sum of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> positive squares for every <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/5/3/153a638e4da1a62fea8e77ac59a66d53c4b9115d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1 \\le k \\le n^2 - 14$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"128\" height=\"19\" />. The impossibility at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/7/c/f7c947ce4ac073137e3527aece1fad6a6d5320d5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k = n^2 - 13$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"95\" height=\"18\" /> (proven above) then sets the limit.\nWe choose **<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/6/2/862eda5c3c04453830638e8ab4e045bdb03903ab.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n = 13$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"52\" height=\"13\" />** (<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/4/e/04e85e716161127c1238215a04e5edd6dff01430.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n^2 = 169$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"72\" height=\"17\" />).\n</p><p>Small <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" />:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/d/5ed8470bc717a49aafe4556c7e2c2e11ddc7b687.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"42\" height=\"13\" />: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/3/5/5357f3621162ab23c1f5df68be44708e47a8ba9e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$169 = 13^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"79\" height=\"17\" />.\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/f/6/4f681bd84648c174d45eed0037702cae77ed0686.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k=2$\" width=\"43\" height=\"12\" />: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/e/ade83164f0495481058046a68ad851f86ecf4fe9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$169 = 12^2 + 5^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"118\" height=\"18\" />.\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/5/3359f43f0fd0ed3b672d389374aecd0360921a47.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k=3$\" width=\"43\" height=\"12\" />: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/a/1/1a1b2fdac4a03d263393366001d788cb55862d20.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$169 = 12^2 + 4^2 + 3^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"156\" height=\"18\" />.\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/e/a/eeae143c5c9dbd376ffa1ffa8bdb93a58e8c9889.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k=4$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"43\" height=\"13\" />: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/a/b/5abaadc56fe2ed8cd0241e734ca069add206713f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$169 = 12^2 + 3^2 + 2^2 + 2^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"195\" height=\"18\" />.\nLarge <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" />: For <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/e/c9ea0eb19264eb885be7c357487274b0606d36c7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5 \\le k \\le 169 - 14$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"137\" height=\"17\" />, Lagrange's Four-Square Theorem guarantees a representation with at most 4 squares. By splitting terms (replacing <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/6/b/76b2878564ab19b80abb21ba964abe90fe120846.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^2$\" width=\"16\" height=\"15\" /> with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/6/b/76b2878564ab19b80abb21ba964abe90fe120846.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^2$\" width=\"16\" height=\"15\" /> ones), we can increase the number of terms arbitrarily up to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/0/6006bba637eef443381fbaff768fa62d9ff41e62.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"17\" />, barring the specific gaps identified in Part (a). Since the gap <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/4/5/f459af4b6495941ea03dd7296af90bb3b47e6309.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\Delta = 13$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"59\" height=\"14\" /> is the smallest gap <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/0/4/f040b184e0e6eaa9464f09c389a6f60fcf1f27c4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$&gt;0$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"27\" height=\"13\" /> that breaks the \"step-down\" chain from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/0/6006bba637eef443381fbaff768fa62d9ff41e62.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"17\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/3/d/83d926786ebc2db8cc70fccbf0a17efc558cfe96.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k=n^2-14$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"95\" height=\"18\" /> corresponds to gap 14 (which is valid as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/6/b160893aaf224770bb5402709a74965c401ec667.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8+3+3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"74\" height=\"15\" />), the sequence holds.\n</p><p>Thus, for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/8/608f4cbd198d2af6bf20b99fc5e126469e09ec84.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n=13$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"52\" height=\"13\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/7/b/67bbf2269829098ace54330ac9f1912fc2a8bd57.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S(n) = 13^2 - 14$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"129\" height=\"21\" />.\n</p><p>Problem (c)\nWe consider integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/3/b/93b0cd0e4226853aa7497c62ecc2ea0181109137.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n = p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"44\" height=\"11\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> is a prime such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/3/0/6303632ce83fd70b9d7c4b40b680a67e6fe9b04e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p \\equiv 1 \\pmod 4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"117\" height=\"20\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/7/fc72315e022cbb43211ed75b82a02512f2ea1ff7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p &gt; 13$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"53\" height=\"17\" />.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/f/6/4f681bd84648c174d45eed0037702cae77ed0686.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k=2$\" width=\"43\" height=\"12\" />: Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/3/0/6303632ce83fd70b9d7c4b40b680a67e6fe9b04e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p \\equiv 1 \\pmod 4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"117\" height=\"20\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> is a sum of two squares <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/f/6/cf669d58fbd0410ca860758e53606d06425a4d97.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a^2+b^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"53\" height=\"16\" />. Then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/4/5/f45a6145e789d5b019eeac3653ec49f5d53f5f97.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n^2 = (a^2-b^2)^2 + (2ab)^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"191\" height=\"21\" />. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> is prime, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/f/4/af40dd462cfac9a98f63c84a474236829d0b3c25.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a \\neq b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"43\" height=\"18\" />, so both terms are non-zero.\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/5/3359f43f0fd0ed3b672d389374aecd0360921a47.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k=3$\" width=\"43\" height=\"12\" />: By Legendre's Three-Square Theorem, a number is a sum of 3 squares unless it is of the form <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/e/efec582de07ebe22856e1df218f7ce19dc800f3a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4^a(8m+7)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"89\" height=\"20\" />. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/6/5/8659295258d587b3223eee8f1cbe7e458b12e896.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p^2 \\equiv 1 \\pmod 8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"124\" height=\"21\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/0/6006bba637eef443381fbaff768fa62d9ff41e62.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"17\" /> is not of this form. The only exceptions for positive squares are a finite set of small integers (the largest is 130). Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/7/fc72315e022cbb43211ed75b82a02512f2ea1ff7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p &gt; 13$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"53\" height=\"17\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/7/0/7705722fce447906c950c443c8c3a644c6767954.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n^2 &gt; 169$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"72\" height=\"18\" />, avoiding these exceptions.\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/6/9f6ac472f19141dc7e30aec12019de3d23847e58.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k \\ge 4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"43\" height=\"15\" />: Always possible. The upper bound on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/6/0965bf432b818b46740e3cd4d042899628c7ad0e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S(n)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"35\" height=\"18\" /> is determined solely by the Frobenius gap <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/4/5/f459af4b6495941ea03dd7296af90bb3b47e6309.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\Delta = 13$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"59\" height=\"14\" /> derived in Part (a), which is independent of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> provided <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> is large enough to contain the squares summing to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/4/e/24ec70ab1de52105778b3ab2540072070aff9c16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\Delta=13$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"59\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>Since there are infinitely many primes <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/3/0/6303632ce83fd70b9d7c4b40b680a67e6fe9b04e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p \\equiv 1 \\pmod 4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"117\" height=\"20\" />, there are infinitely many such integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1992_IMO_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"clear:both; margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1992_IMO\" title=\"1992 IMO\">1992 IMO</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1992_IMO_Problems\" title=\"1992 IMO Problems\">Problems</a></b>) • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c3222\">Resources</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"33%\" align=\"center\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1992_IMO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1992 IMO Problems/Problem 5\">Problem 5</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"34%\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1992_IMO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1992 IMO Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1992_IMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1992 IMO Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1992_IMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1992 IMO Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1992_IMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1992 IMO Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1992_IMO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1992 IMO Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">6</a>\n</td>\n<td width=\"33%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b>Last Question</b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=IMO_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"IMO Problems and Solutions\"> All IMO Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017183431\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.035 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.049 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 517/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 86